My third shift at the café was finally over.
It has been a very busy Saturday.
I washed the large wooden counter clean.
Afterwards, I went out into the staff room.
I took off my apron.
I hung it on the first hook on the wall.
I have learned a whole lot on my first shifts.
I have finally learned to froth milk correctly.
I have also learned to remember a regular customer's order.
It has been fun, but I was also a bit tired.
I took my bag from the table.
Then I walked out to the front door.
I locked the door securely with the key.
I stepped out onto the street.
The afternoon sun was shining brightly over the city.
I smiled to myself on the way to the bus.
I am very happy with my new volunteer work.
I am already looking forward to my fourth shift.
